Claude DesktopClaude CodeChatGPT <p>Open Settings &gt; Developer &gt; Edit Config and add to <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code>:</p> <pre><code>{
    "mcpServers": {
        "aurastream": {
            "command": "aurastream-mcp",
            "env": {
                "AURASTREAM_API_KEY": "YOUR_AURASTREAM_API_KEY"
            }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <p>Restart Claude Desktop. If the command is not found, use its full path.</p> <pre><code>claude mcp add aurastream -e AURASTREAM_API_KEY=YOUR_AURASTREAM_API_KEY -- aurastream-mcp
</code></pre> <p>Add <code>-e FRED_API_KEY=...</code> and similar for sources that need credentials.</p> <p>ChatGPT connects to remote MCP servers over HTTPS. Run the server in HTTP mode:</p> <pre><code>AURASTREAM_API_KEY=YOUR_AURASTREAM_API_KEY aurastream-mcp --http --port 8000 --allowed-host mcp.example.com
</code></pre> <p>Expose it at a public HTTPS address (a reverse proxy with TLS, or a tunnel such as Cloudflare Tunnel or ngrok) and add <code>https://mcp.example.com/mcp</code> as a connector in ChatGPT.</p> <p>HTTP mode is for single-user self-hosting</p> <p>A client that sends an <code>x-api-key</code> or <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> header uses its own key. Without one, the server falls back to <code>AURASTREAM_API_KEY</code>, so anyone with the URL uses your allowance and your provider credentials. Keep the URL private, or start the server with <code>--require-client-key</code>.</p>
